{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","commitSha":"c2534ff9c84422e00711da31629a76f3f59feb98","shard":"2aa2265839efd1b4","symbols":[{"path":"xrpl/TaggedPointer","kind":"class","name":"TaggedPointer","qualifiedName":"xrpl::TaggedPointer","scope":"xrpl","category":"production","access":"public","documentation":{"status":"present","brief":[{"type":"link","text":"TaggedPointer","target":{"path":"xrpl/TaggedPointer","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"type":"text","text":" is a combination of a pointer and a mask stored in the lowest two bits."}],"description":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Since pointers do not have arbitrary alignment, the lowest bits in the pointer are guaranteed to be zero. "},{"type":"link","text":"TaggedPointer","target":{"path":"xrpl/TaggedPointer","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"type":"text","text":" stores information in these low bits. When dereferencing the pointer, these low \"tag\" bits are set to zero. When accessing the tag bits, the high \"pointer\" bits are set to zero."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The \"pointer\" part points to the equivalent to an array of "},{"type":"code","text":"SHAMapHash"},{"type":"text","text":" followed immediately by an array of "},{"type":"code","text":"shared_ptr<SHAMapTreeNode>"},{"type":"text","text":". The sizes of these arrays are determined by the tag. The tag is an index into an array ("},{"type":"code","text":"boundaries"},{"type":"text","text":", defined in the cpp file) that specifies the size. Both arrays are the same size. Note that the sizes may be smaller than the full 16 elements needed to explicitly store all the children. In this case, the arrays only store the non-empty children. The non-empty children are stored in index order. For example, if only children "},{"type":"code","text":"2"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"code","text":"14"},{"type":"text","text":" are non-empty, a two-element array would store child "},{"type":"code","text":"2"},{"type":"text","text":" in array index 0 and child "},{"type":"code","text":"14"},{"type":"text","text":" in array index 1. There are functions to convert between a child's tree index and the child's index in a sparse array."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The motivation for this class is saving RAM. A large percentage of inner nodes only store a small number of children. Memory can be saved by storing the inner node's children in sparse arrays. Measurements show that on average a typical "},{"type":"link","text":"SHAMap","target":{"path":"xrpl/SHAMap","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"type":"text","text":"'s inner nodes can be stored using only 25% of the original space."}]}],"returns":null,"notes":[],"suppressionReason":null,"inheritedFrom":null},"location":{"declaration":{"file":"include/xrpl/shamap/detail/TaggedPointer.h","line":43},"definition":{"file":"include/xrpl/shamap/detail/TaggedPointer.h","line":44,"endLine":227}},"corrections":[],"templateParameters":null,"isTemplateSpecialization":false,"isFinal":false,"isAbstract":false,"baseClasses":[],"derivedClasses":[],"friends":[],"deductionGuides":[],"nested":["xrpl/TaggedPointer/RawAllocateTag"],"members":["xrpl/TaggedPointer/tp_","xrpl/TaggedPointer/kTagMask","xrpl/TaggedPointer/kPtrMask","xrpl/TaggedPointer/destroyHashesAndChildren/0e56862f","xrpl/TaggedPointer/TaggedPointer/f3634d12","xrpl/TaggedPointer/TaggedPointer/deeeacac","xrpl/TaggedPointer/TaggedPointer/398bb675","xrpl/TaggedPointer/TaggedPointer/a93c371e","xrpl/TaggedPointer/TaggedPointer/fead613a","xrpl/TaggedPointer/TaggedPointer/521acbca","xrpl/TaggedPointer/TaggedPointer/747cbb64","xrpl/TaggedPointer/operator-assign/39e233bd","xrpl/TaggedPointer/~TaggedPointer/758b45dc","xrpl/TaggedPointer/decode/2ed3818a","xrpl/TaggedPointer/capacity/c62bde87","xrpl/TaggedPointer/isDense/5a0f7dba","xrpl/TaggedPointer/getHashesAndChildren/e29f50c4","xrpl/TaggedPointer/getHashes/48cf772c","xrpl/TaggedPointer/getChildren/95cb258a","xrpl/TaggedPointer/iterChildre